# qubes-win-idd — SINGLE authoritative policy for the Windows test rig.
#
# Numbered 10- ON PURPOSE: qrexec stops at the FIRST match, and the rig already has
# 29-win-idd-testbed, 30-win-idd-dev, 30-win-idd-fullscreen, 31-win-idd-clone,
# 31-win-idd-mgmt and 31-win-idd-resize. Evaluating this file first makes every grant
# below authoritative regardless of what those contain, so no archaeology is needed and
# no later deny/ask can shadow it.
#
# It is a SUPERSET of what those six grant to win-idd-mgmt (admin API + qubes.VMShell/
# VMExec/Filecopy + the local.Win* dom0 helpers), so once this is verified the older files
# can be deleted. Deleting them is optional — leaving them costs nothing but clutter.
#
# Service names were enumerated from the installed qubesadmin client, which found the two
# real defects in the current setup:
#   * admin.vm.Create.standalone  is not a service. The real name is
#     admin.vm.Create.StandaloneVM  -> VM creation/cloning could never have worked.
#   * admin.Events was left commented out in 06-install-mgmt-policy.sh. Its absence does
#     not error, it makes qvm-* HANG (measured: qvm-ls blocking >120 s).
#
# Scope: source is always win-idd-mgmt. Destinations are only the test guests (by either
# tag they carry), win-idd-mgmt itself (to enumerate the loop devices it exports), and dom0
# (calls with no target VM). Nothing else on the system is touched.
#
# NOT granted, deliberately: admin.property.Set (global defaults), admin.pool.Add/.Remove
# (storage pools), admin.backup.* .

## ===== admin API on the test guests (both tags; new/cloned VMs get created-by-* automatically) =====
